# let-go version for building xsofy — single source of truth.
# deploy-pages.yml and the test.yml floor lane both resolve the version from here.
#
# v1.13.0 carries everything the web bundle depends on:
#   - #378 renames the -w-shell none host mount #terminal -> #app and ships it
#     visible; the shell (tools/xsofy-shell.html) binds #app. Shipped in v1.12.2.
#   - #245 (client-owned shell) and #339 (js/url-param host seam), from v1.11.1.
#   - #859 makes vm.Int 64 bits on every host and #862 lowers a let-go :int to
#     int64. Both are no-ops for this bundle: they only widen 32-bit-int hosts
#     (linux/386, TinyGo wasm), and stock Go wasm was already 64-bit. Existing
#     seeds name the same worlds.
#
# This was a bare commit SHA (cf195a67, #378 itself) from 2026-07-16, when no
# release carried #378 yet. v1.12.2 shipped it on 2026-07-20, so the SHA is no
# longer needed — and it had gone stale: a bundle built with it fails to boot,
# dying at namespace load with
#   error loading xsofy.input: calling dev? — bit-shift-left expected Int
# The floor lane cannot see that: its WASM step builds the bundle but never
# boots one, and this failure is at namespace load, not at build. Nothing
# shipped broken: deploy-pages.yml fires only on v* tags, and the last one
# predates the SHA pin.
v1.13.0
